    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15696" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">emprosthŏtŏnĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπροσθοτονία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a disease in which the limbs are drawn forward and
				stiffen</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Acut. 3, 6,
			61</span></i>.—The same called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">empro-sthŏtŏnos</span></b>  (=<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπροσθότονος</span>) morbus, <i><span class="en">id. ib.
				3, 6, 65</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">emprosthŏtŏ-nĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπροσθοτονικός</span>, <i>suffering from
				this disease</i>, <i><span class="en">id. ib.</span></i> § 69.</div>
